139 registers, 8.7KB smem. No spills. Good. Let me think about occupancy: with 139 registers, 256 threads/block = 35584 regs/block. A40 has 65536 regs per SM. So ~1 block per SM from registers? 65536/35584 = 1.8, so 1 block (256 threads). With 8736 bytes smem, sm_80 has... shared memory per SM is 100KB (opt-in 164KB). 8736 bytes → many blocks possible from smem. So register-limited to 1 block (256 threads) per SM → only 256 threads/SM, that's low occupancy and might limit latency hiding.

Let me reduce register usage to get more occupancy, or increase work per thread (which increases registers but reduces block count).

